The file `callweb` is generated test input, not a copy of a third-party program.

It is the output of a seeded, offline program generator: the `callweb` generator
of the `gors-bins-generators` suite at recipe version `gen-1`, seed `callweb-s9`.
The generator emits Rust source with a deliberately dense call graph, and it
downloads nothing.

Build:

    rustc 1.98.0
    target     armv7-unknown-linux-gnueabihf
    flags      opt-level=z, panic=abort, lto=fat, codegen-units=1, strip
    result     ELF32 little-endian EM_ARM, PIE, stripped, 289648 bytes
    sha256     2e35cfc59b74d0af516875535ac1f6f915e1733327647c1fc52213be0c175da5

