Compiling that source statically links the Rust standard library as shipped with
rustc 1.98.0, so this file carries code the Rust project distributes as well.
All 40 of the `/rustc/<hash>/library/` source paths left in its panic metadata
name commit 88d9e12ae178fab0fb5cc050a94da85685d449ea, which is release 1.98.0.
The backtrace dependencies vendored into that standard library leave their
version strings in the file too: addr2line 0.25.1, gimli 0.32.3, miniz_oxide
0.8.9 and rustc-demangle 0.1.27. The Rust Project is dual-licensed under
Apache 2.0 and MIT terms, and tracks the licenses of the components vendored
into it in https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/master/COPYRIGHT
